  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the tomatoes as the subject of the educational claim",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any deictic pronoun like 'you' or 'me'. However, the meme implicitly projects the user onto the tomatoes as the entity being described — the tomatoes are the subject of the claim 'proof you can be a fruit and a vegetable'. The user is invited to identify with the tomatoes as the example of something that can simultaneously be both a fruit and a vegetable, making the tomatoes the projected entity. The user is not projected onto the text itself, but onto the visual material (tomatoes) which the text is describing.",
